# fixedbugs, defect 568, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R3).
#
# SYMPTOM: `sched_getcpu` bound from glibc's `sched.h` with no switch was told
# *`sched.h` declares no `sched_getcpu`*, which is false: it declares it under
# `_GNU_SOURCE`, and nothing told the author where the switch can stand. This
# header hides its function as glibc does.
#
# FIX: a refused round asks the module's headers again under each switch,
# `_XOPEN_SOURCE` then `_GNU_SOURCE`, defined before every header
# (`cli/switch_ask.hero`), and a name declared there is told as hidden, with
# the one place the switch can stand.

extern "fixedbugs-568-a-name-a-header-declares-only-under-a-switch-is-told-so.h"
    function hidden_cpu() -> i32  #~ ffi_unknown_name

function main()
    print(hidden_cpu() >= 0)
